    "TREATMENT": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Usually not life-threatening, but pyelonephritis and cyst involvement warrant immediate measures to prevent sepsis and mortality.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Most cysts increase in size and number, often impairing adjacent renal parenchyma.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Elimination of renal cysts is not yet feasible; treatment is limited to minimizing the consequences of renal cyst formation (i.e., CKD, infection, hematuria, and pain).",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Removing fluid from large cysts may minimize pain and compression of adjacent renal parenchyma. This procedure is impractical in kidneys with multiple large cysts.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "A vasopressin antagonist (tolvaptan), has been shown to slow kidney enlargement and slow decline in kidney function in people with AD-PKD.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Some patients require treatment for concomitant CKD.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Consider nephrectomy only if infected cysts are associated with uncontrollable sepsis.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Disease eradication by selective breeding of unaffected cats may be impossible because ~40% of Persians are affected.",
          "pdf_page": 1187,
          "printed_page": 1105,
          "column": 2
        }
      ],
